Z||000000||phillip||04-03-2000||08:41 AM||||<BR>i'd like to to switch the rear lower (below the black band) section of my '87 coupe to a gt rear. if i can't find the rounded trim do you think it's possible to maybe sand down the ribbed trim to round it out? i know where one ribbed style is if i can get the guy to sell it. is '86 or '87 the 1st year it changed?||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||04-03-2000||11:51 AM||||It has the round on 86-88 GT's. The 86-87 SE's retained the older style moldings.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-03-2000||12:48 PM||||The 86 and 87 SE has same back as GT but ribbed.  All GT's are smooth. If you want you can swap all the trim for smooth. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||04-03-2000||06:34 PM||||Except the '85 GT, which is ribbed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||04-03-2000||06:39 PM||||Yep, you are correct monkey, my 85 GT has ribbed molding... but the 87 coupe i have junked for parts has the smooth trim..||||reg||3
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||04-03-2000||09:10 PM||||The molding is molded into the rear fascia. The only way to swap moldings on the fascias is to get a fascia with the molding you want.<BR>||||reg||1
